  "question": "Does the publicly excerpted 1950-02-11 Song Yunbin diary entry close or reconcile the early Tieqin Tongjian Lou purchase/donation counts recorded in the existing Gu Tinglong, Deng Zhicheng and later Ji Shuying-derived controls?",
  "answer": "It adds a distinct contemporaneous diary report but does not close reconciliation. A public excerpt explicitly headed 1950-02-11 reports Song Yunbin recording Zhao Wanli's account that the government/Culture Ministry paid thirty million yuan for 302 Tieqin titles and that the Qu family separately donated 52 titles. CiNii and university catalog records independently close the 2016 Zhonghua Shuju three-volume edition identity, while Zhejiang archival authorities close the upstream Song Yunbin diary manuscript corpus as archival holdings. However, the exact 2016 page and manuscript leaf for 1950-02-11 have not been directly reviewed. The Song figures differ from the publication-mediated Gu Tinglong Jan-6 control (300 purchased, 42 donated) and the later Ji Shuying-derived recounting (304 sold, 52 donated), while the Deng Jan-29 control uses a different unit and amount (twelve boxes, forty million). These differences may reflect reporting time, counting scope, transaction stage, editorial/transcription variation or distinct transactions. No silent normalization is authorized.",
